tasks.details:
Scope: apps/web/src (pages and components). The catalogue lives in apps/web/messages/*.json.

Out of scope: the API (its error strings are English by design and are translated on the frontend), the docs, and the demo data generator.

Definition of done:
  - the scanner reports zero hard-coded English strings in the pages that were touched;
  - all nine locale files carry the same key set (the parity check is clean);
  - npx tsc --noEmit, npx eslint src and npx jest --silent stay green;
  - a visitor who switches the locale sees the page body change, not only the navigation.

Property.currency already exists (apps/api/data/schemas.py:110) and the demo catalogue ships PLN, but four places still assume a dollar or a euro:
- components/search/heatmap-legend.tsx hard-codes the dollar sign;
- components/analytics/area-comparison.tsx:56 hard-codes $$;
- the area insights in apps/api/api/routers/market.py return no currency;
- apps/api/api/routers/valuation.py:87 defaults to "EUR".
All of them route through formatPrice(value, currency, locale) in apps/web/src/lib/format.ts, and the API returns the currency of the listing.

THE COPY MUST MATCH THE DATA
The prototype's Data and coverage section says "prices in each listing's own currency (zl, EUR, GBP, USD)". The seeded catalogue is PLN only. Either the seed grows a second currency or the copy is softened to what the catalogue holds - and whichever it is, the catalogue stats endpoint reports the real currency mix instead of the page asserting four currencies.

The Data and coverage table itself (Poland with a demo catalogue in five cities plus a live provider with your own key; the EU, the UK and the US planned; anywhere else a data source away) is copied from the prototype and stays honest: the enrichment adapters - OpenStreetMap points of interest, safety, noise, transport, air quality - are country-agnostic, and the air-quality adapter has static fallbacks for the major Polish cities.
